  "name": "Robot-joint outrunner 40p/36s (Electronics 2023)",
  "description": "The 36-slot / 40-pole outer-rotor robot-joint motor of Zhang et al., Electronics 12(2):397 (2023), Table 1: 76.4 mm stator, 58.5 mm hub bore, 7 mm stack, 2 mm teeth, 0.5 mm air gap, 1.8 mm magnets at a 0.88 pole arc, 13 turns per tooth coil (26 conductors per slot here, since two tooth coils share each slot). The tooth shoes (2.5 mm mouth, 0.7 mm deep) are read from the paper's cross-section. Catalog N35 (Br 1.23 T) stands in for N38SH and M350-50A for the 20WTG1500 steel. The paper measured 7.3 V peak line back-EMF at 600 rpm and 0.21 N·m at 1.27 A rms with id = 0. Those two imply magnet flux linkages about 16% apart, so no model matches both: coilEM lands between them, about 9% above the back-EMF and 7% below the torque. Published hardware data, not a coilEM benchmark: there is no pass/fail.",
  "schema_version": "1.0",
